WEBVTT

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:11.180
With the increasing application of AI technology, there is a growing concern that it may negatively impact human creativity.
随着人工智能技术的应用日益广泛，越来越多的人担心它可能会对人类的创造力产生负面影响。

00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:20.810
Now that AI can write poems, compose music and create paintings in seconds, some people fear that we will gradually stop thinking for ourselves.
既然人工智能几秒钟就能写诗、作曲、绘画，一些人担心我们会逐渐不再独立思考。

00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:23.430
This concern is not groundless.
这种担忧并非毫无根据。

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:36.540
When a ready-made answer is just a click away, students may be tempted to let AI write their essays instead of struggling with their own ideas, yet it is exactly through such struggle that creativity grows.
当现成的答案只需点一下鼠标就能得到时，学生可能会忍不住让人工智能替他们写作文，而不去苦苦琢磨自己的想法；然而，恰恰是通过这样的苦思，创造力才得以成长。

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:41.740
Over time, overreliance on AI could weaken our imagination.
久而久之，过度依赖人工智能可能会削弱我们的想象力。

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:44.510
However, AI is not the enemy.
然而，人工智能并不是敌人。

00:00:45.310 --> 00:00:50.390
Used wisely, it can free us from repetitive work and offer fresh inspiration.
如果运用得当，它能把我们从重复性的工作中解放出来，并带来新的灵感。

00:00:51.190 --> 00:00:59.890
A designer, for instance, can generate dozens of sketches with AI and then devote more time to refining the most original one.
例如，设计师可以用人工智能生成几十幅草图，然后把更多时间用来完善其中最有创意的那一幅。

00:01:00.690 --> 00:01:03.740
The key, therefore, lies in how we use AI.
因此，关键在于我们如何使用人工智能。

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:12.790
We should treat it as an assistant rather than a substitute, using it to explore possibilities while keeping the final judgment in our own hands.
我们应该把它当作助手而不是替代品，用它来探索各种可能性，同时把最终的判断权掌握在自己手中。

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:18.750
Schools should encourage students to think independently before turning to AI for help.
学校应该鼓励学生先独立思考，再求助于人工智能。

00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:24.350
In this way, AI can enrich human creativity instead of replacing it.
这样，人工智能就能丰富人类的创造力，而不是取代它。
